{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_588a7c859133f273b0cff80a2f3b1b70077d50aa75b2336ddd8293c4e71296c6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1ad8d01896c97ba250c88366dff90bdd8ebb021bfba50fdaab4c439cce93da1f","slc_70ff56abb0846a40642fe7d299464638c07227415c40cfe56a7383faa6de9be2","slc_9f155914268d682aa9cf58ebf792b3e00053f17981ac1c77c2b87dd89ff69d4f","slc_ff86193af6a85b9dada5b511882e759f7f8d40d0d95c32f9bc703ee0039f4283"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"The design mandates graceful degradation so memory is never a single point of failure: FTS failure leads to rebuild then substring fallback, writeback failure is skipped, and a disabled memory subsystem leaves the normal agent loop intact.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_63567129734f146b1d51efb17811a6838506f397b13556fbf09fe84b80287d2f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a41139dba23d82efdb18f9fe7dcdbf2ada15f2f318bb85964d6ef13a9751240","slc_0d58e451e7a3fd2166bb2c10986e0b9a88ed5d61876fc406807057a68e4b4ded","slc_7b02cee427b55b1d8b44b785596d22ebf62207ebfd419c79252db14948e04bcc","slc_8704e611067ca5a2635ca54ba7bd37e3c643e45690ed3d6c90df3993a9e7f7c5","slc_e940a69ad6b982a8dccf95b9afbc95369a51caaf02cf0908d0b6683653d964a7"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"Chinese-text retrieval is handled by pre-segmenting with Node's native Intl.Segmenter (zh, word granularity) into the FTS search_text, while canonical content keeps the original text; if segmentation is unavailable, unicode61 plus substring fallback is used.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_67591fa88eca82da71e254d7e0fb5bb48276b96048f06b2f4cf036026b608808","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8629d3e9c553c571f7e4befb24f6b1017b1903f0f30e710e287228c2e3bc1b11"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"The repository contains a design RFC (status: Design RFC) scoped to Codemini CLI / WebUI / Agent Runtime, proposing a memory subsystem with SQLite FTS5 + BM25 as default retrieval and embeddings explicitly optional.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_76471ab999d41388d8657f3b86b3fb872196e9360c2388a86c66024f301d69c8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_38c27d9fa51ef46137688203673979765c2958e7ff24fcc78337026aa77ced46","slc_5d7db57691630f5c302c1aee223adc67e860aba4628a8e111be0996fe5850769","slc_6493dbee2e45ea3768d0a07f6cc150476990e6107b603ad2c7355b2328f3b464","slc_7460a3812c693e03db74e35925297b23e5ac86034f090e105e8b6222904a0d85","slc_7fc66cd05484bcc3bb19c2dcc3a63fdc8e059d3e698fb7ee3d65ef59a4fdd381","slc_b3a6877db03dd253c7a1c5ef50cdcaec7c6106d34a4eb51e199c90ba12a99ffe"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"A unified MemoryRetrievalAdapter interface is specified with search, upsert, remove, and rebuild methods; the default implementation is FTS5RetrievalAdapter, with a HybridRetrievalAdapter mentioned as a possible future extension.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7c7be0fa0a0792cb48537eeb61fdb4224e7ac1b347035b9a1b4aa002baf387c9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_06b37138904bd90ae85585d68ca02edd8b6ec9971bcc290ee2f0163aaa7d49fb","slc_22cc16297c7bad33c15f3cd61c474b66d6c2865b0abcf729da2aa0c0489cd025","slc_4b9ad6ae4f961520a228ac106f922eaa927bc78f0ab1aa0293d681f7e174f01b","slc_67eb32905fc52a774b2cb80b429bb4c99aeb3a7978348269204a560fdfbfc41c","slc_89389345aeae4d38d1bf55d7244a418887c102561e482fe700ceb1cd19b36f16","slc_f25e97caad98e9e906786d783d00500bf84240b00bb9dfe1bb89529d247644ce"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"Three recall paths are specified: bootstrap recall injecting a small stable profile at session start, per-turn recall of top 3-5 repo/coding/procedure memories, and failure-triggered recall of 1-3 coding memories after a tool failure; retrieval before every tool call is explicitly discouraged.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7fe49ddae134949dea32796528999879ef0ec76ae331200b8be06432dbb0f21f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0ead88eecd9d524a4e2f7a639524fdfa01b8e2f0e6631573ffedfaa7ff841e49","slc_0fba3f33190dd1d1735a523521394ed094ace6a3c1861b2f9bcdb642e2604a75","slc_85626489d02ec6ad0fcfd275d713e7bea9f28c90f895a0a0ec5e7b00900df2cd","slc_95c44bcf896a5ecb6538fb58dcd09b1fabe924244c4dcead41169616ecc69731","slc_d3ffba1a49ee8590703bb422db7160d75577ce3bb36d831bd2ccd91ffe867c26","slc_d7731180f3f989bd989b9da02548bce11c0f5fdcbfbc92fe5671b9867e600247"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"Canonical memory is the single source of truth; the FTS retrieval index is derived data that must be rebuildable when corrupted, without affecting the memory itself.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_80a9555406e787020f7d5065dd8b3a09326de0c0abb2a297f3e31a804fe99ae3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_965ec7b3f9d7dbdf56a79188639783bec634358f816c995453b6f078bd4216d3","slc_b64edf463af241d9e1a8f70707bba02281fe4227d6fcc019f040a0203db5f711","slc_d147ca229d1ca1e0de200fbcfca4e231103abfa3c42d985a2b8a7c34e3c6fbdd","slc_ec80597d73fe65f10f9e866de5e90ea8e170048195428b958bc3d28abd31247f"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"The architecture separates understanding from retrieval: the LLM judges what is worth remembering, extracts atomic facts, classifies scope/family/kind, and detects conflicts, while FTS5/BM25 handles retrieval, filtering, ranking, and top-K recall; embeddings are not relied on by default.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_981fd41c2f871b8eeca1d771e0087c16c838d49219bab39635015a7dcfd6921c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9003bc5b25a930cfcfd00d4f9ecf2210d48e187710184959230af2420045c0fd"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"The design targets four goals: cross-session memory, task-relevant recall rather than stuffing all memory into the prompt, learning reusable engineering experience from failure-to-verification cycles, and long-term governance (dedup, expiry, conflict handling, eviction).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b6f242e1b03985c0a39ef933636482c724b96dd542bc2462c075b9f52430973d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_081b9824c290a084dddae69363c463dfd8168d3ef85ee924bf1cde92258acce7","slc_613893d8f4224d179a95807f47113060d63852cccca026904ed42716423bbcf2","slc_69d1c49092377c12571cae00761c3e3c5e3445422cb92aad0e56fcde0fd4d269","slc_86c253fb0fb07873ff33bebac86c1216bd78f70a41d0d9e2c2e7ce59adcb6b72"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"Storage is local-first: user/global memories go in codemini.sqlite, while project memories live in <repo>/.codemini/index.sqlite alongside the repository, avoiding global absolute-path mapping.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e9238398b75f82ae956eb6a9d096302ea36cc6e1699b19aa0bf939d3d08031f6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_138de303d1039f69ee42968c2826e345e95adb61c5f0a0632bd88eb032de4d18","slc_a031f5732c5563950c5f083a30e6dd3bbe6683bba838edf84a3d5bd04ef6c67a","slc_a185a77e64224123845fa462c2892820548534b691eaac08d78da134898e8723","slc_b5770be2809bffbe196ebe4e663b5149de69544e91d355ad26590a83eb8f1fa8","slc_e5a75adbc514b33106416a22c20dcb5228ef628ebdca59b3c8194a83cbc11f94"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"Memory records are typed along three orthogonal dimensions: scope (user/global/project), family (personal/repo/coding/procedure), and kind (preference/convention/lesson/note).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ede699310232f10c3cb894f289da582653ff1ef7bfee6ecb1efb7e2d44a732ef","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03f226883bd2b2064691654e8e4ff00201692e74e69bb2be1004dc50307de82d","slc_06563efed9d5db643ac9416622ce6f88a32ff2c7388f44a4126e01d9e312b3d8","slc_36ccdc0881f25d9ca9ae4d93fee241237edcc156361e125952e30778caf08efc","slc_4e97a2df88b3f26e2bccce856f345b1afa8121a0dd38b0b06cb1525dce679ff9","slc_6a14b08674de123dc356c7993fa4f162e0f9c47f87528ffacb0aa78a9693fdbd","slc_756e57a3a82ff224520204bdb29fa310d844492963028460efcbd04e7b457f30","slc_f990ef8aff529317b22c07876c15a69a320eb110c477d6aec02d1b2f32c04d85"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"A proposed MemoryRecord interface includes lifecycle (operational/longterm/archived), confidence, source/session/branch metadata, counters for confirmations, accesses, successes and failures, expected validity days, pinned flag, and revision number.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fd80a5674ec93833de497ea6bd01db01080cacdeb4f0bf6c10c9741159f6aace","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"havingautism/codemini-cli@3e3a6665c9d2 snapshot f27607039cb943e9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d5b004262f928766b3e7a767dfa41f6bc903287fd3175b39a8c5b6eff7a8757","slc_44abc598df3a510d2cf64e15df12439a74c22307bb4bfa5e89562a7949aa2791","slc_961cef1097b09f3d9b724b38eba4b93132ffa5178dd610ca1693855a7c939b19","slc_e27456109a19d19336c90f7b21d874d335aa481643ddd0af4c6cf34da50a5747","slc_f2dddea7562498042215f0497c0d69f8ff9577977b79cebc4ba9bc1ce5fd7e47"],"source_ids":["src_3fbdf62866815843a69214e39c9f8001"],"text":"First-version retrieval ranking is a weighted blend: BM25 relevance 70%, confidence 15%, verification 10%, recency 5%, with project exact-scope applied as a filter rather than a soft weight; retrieval score and long-term retention score are kept as separate concepts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a090432cf1024b07bd72145317ef1772"}
